  "id": "COMPOUND:24024 - PROTEIN:5942",
  "verbalization": "Callyspongenol B appears to interact with Tankyrase-2 through a series of intermediate targets, including Carboxylesterase 2 and Raji, which in turn target (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol. This compound is known to act as a target of Tankyrase-2, suggesting a potential regulatory role in the enzyme's function. The evidence suggests that Callyspongenol B may modulate Tankyrase-2 activity by influencing the expression or function of its downstream targets. The overlapping pathways and the consistent presence of (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol as a common intermediate support a mechanism where Callyspongenol B indirectly affects Tankyrase-2 through these intermediaries. The integration of multiple paths highlights a potential regulatory network involving Tankyrase-2, with Callyspongenol B acting as a modulator of this pathway.",
